Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Patients admitted  [OR] to the intensive care unit for more than 48 hours or admitted in the hospital for more than seven days
  -  Presence of any of the invasive devices (endotracheal tube, [OR]  central venous catheter  [OR] or urinary catheters) before randomization  [AND] and absence of the intention to exchange the devices;
  -  Previous use of any type of coated devices;
  -  Age < 18 years;
  -  Known pregnancy
  -  Known allergy to gold, silver  [OR] and palladium;
  -  Suspected  [OR] or confirmed brain death;
  -  Previously enrolled in the study
Newly added exclusion criteria in version 2
